{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793020501,"nonce":"DiHu22Od3dRqZ3jG5OlejZqGv4M=","message":"Implemented in db392ec (Isolate browser recovery by workspace and account).\n\nNative sessions persist opaque host/workspace recovery IDs privately outside the repository, publish a versioned cacheIdentity in hello and verified auth.login, and rotate the workspace recovery ID when the document-state directory is reset. Random IDs are atomically published across concurrent starters; malformed IDs fail startup. The Cloudflare Durable Object stamps its logical workspace/account ownership while retaining the compute document-state generation. Until DO document authority is implemented, a fresh compute disk must change the recovery context rather than merge an old replica into a new baseline.\n\nThe browser keys IndexedDB documents and personal workspace metadata by the verified context, authenticates before recovery, and fences changed workspaces/accounts/state generations before CRDT sync. Existing recovery data stays preserved. Legacy unscoped caches are not automatically imported; legacy servers disable durable recovery. Sign-in serializes new document opens and prevents a disconnect during credential verification from becoming ready. Full editor bindings become read-only and report replacement; process handles remain disconnected.\n\nValidation: native session suite 34 passing tests; core-only cargo check passed. Browser session suite 34 passed, including real Chrome offline/reload/account isolation and anonymous-to-signed-in recovery. Rust Workers gateway suite 8 passed using pinned worker-build 0.8.7, including repeated handshakes, owner/workspace scope, persistent restart and fresh compute storage. Two full WASM editors passed edits, author-local undo, interrupted Save, offline restart recovery, tab restoration, binding lifecycle and replacement-state write blocking without a runtime error.\n\nRebuilt native session and full WASM bundle; tested bundle staged at bin/web/rayde. Local session restarted at 127.0.0.1:7070 with existing workspace/URL/credentials/environment; read-only live identity and workspace access smoke passed. Served adapter SHA matches tested bundle (80237d46d4eca0a781088e05233475dcbd926819012faf8dd93fe0ca65733962). WASM bbda2e02eed7d5f1df0b044c07f3112728e1b413817ec7e7502f0968ba86884f. Reload the page to pick up the adapter; legacy tab/history namespaces are retained but not trusted for automatic import.\n\nDO document authority, production MSB provisioning and aggregate resource quotas remain open in their parent tracks. A follow-up will present the replacement warning as one themed warning toast card per session rather than repeated per-file status messages, as requested.","files":null}]}